{"pageId":"/pages/examples/@id","routeParams":{"id":"ci-integration"},"data":{"example":{"id":"ci-integration","title":"CI Integration","description":"Demonstrates integrating functional-examples into a CI pipeline\nusing GitHub Actions. The workflow file is annotated with region\ntags for documentation extraction.\n","rootPath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/ci-integration","files":[{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/ci-integration/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","raw":"# CI Integration\n\nDemonstrates integrating functional-examples testing into a GitHub Actions CI pipeline.\n\n## What This Shows\n\n- A GitHub Actions workflow for scanning and testing examples\n- Region-tagged workflow steps for documentation extraction\n- The same `scan` and `test` commands used locally and in CI\n\n## Running\n\n```bash\n# Scan for examples (same command used in CI)\nbash demo.sh\n```\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe `.github/workflows/examples.yml` file defines a real GitHub Actions workflow\nthat installs dependencies, scans for examples, and runs tests. Region tags\n(`#_region`) in the workflow file allow documentation to extract specific steps\nfor inclusion in guides.\n\nPush to GitHub to execute the workflow, or inspect the YAML directly to\nunderstand the CI setup.\n","parsed":"!undefined","hunks":"!undefined","language":"markdown","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-markdown\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">#</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> CI Integration</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">Demonstrates integrating functional-examples testing into a GitHub Actions CI pipeline.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> What This Shows</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> A GitHub Actions workflow for scanning and testing examples</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Region-tagged workflow steps for documentation extraction</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> The same </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">scan</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> and </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">test</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> commands used locally and in CI</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Running</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Scan for examples (same command used in CI)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">bash</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> demo.sh</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> How It Works</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">The </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">.github/workflows/examples.yml</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> file defines a real GitHub Actions workflow</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">that installs dependencies, scans for examples, and runs tests. Region tags</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">(</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">#_region</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">) in the workflow file allow documentation to extract specific steps</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">for inclusion in guides.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">Push to GitHub to execute the workflow, or inspect the YAML directly to</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">understand the CI setup.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>"},{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/ci-integration/demo.sh","relativePath":"demo.sh","raw":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Demonstrates scanning examples in a CI-ready project\n\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\n\n# #_region scan\n# Scan for examples — same command used in the GitHub Actions workflow\nnpx functional-examples scan\n# #_endregion scan\n","parsed":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Demonstrates scanning examples in a CI-ready project\n\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\n\n# Scan for examples — same command used in the GitHub Actions workflow\nnpx functional-examples scan\n","hunks":[{"id":"scan","content":"# Scan for examples — same command used in the GitHub Actions workflow\nnpx functional-examples scan","startLine":6,"endLine":9}],"language":"bash","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\">#!/usr/bin/env bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Demonstrates scanning examples in a CI-ready project</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span st